  "body": "## Related issue\r\n\r\nFixes #7891\r\n\r\n## Problem\r\n\r\n`BaseTool._validate_kwargs` serialized the validated args model with a plain `model_dump()`, so every optional argument the caller never set came back as an explicit `None`. Tools generated by `MCPServerAdapter` forward those values to the MCP server as JSON `null`. A server that validates input against a strict JSON Schema (optional field declared as `{\"type\": \"string\"}`, not nullable) rejects the call, even though the caller left the field unset.\r\n\r\n```python\r\n# optional `nickname` omitted by the caller\r\ngreet_tool.run(name=\"Ada\")\r\n# before: arguments sent to the server -> {\"name\": \"Ada\", \"nickname\": null}   (rejected)\r\n# after:  arguments sent to the server -> {\"name\": \"Ada\"}\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Change\r\n\r\n`_validate_kwargs` (`lib/crewai/src/crewai/tools/base_tool.py`) now drops a field only when **both** hold: the caller did not provide it (`model_fields_set`), and its validated value is `None`. Everything else is unchanged:\r\n\r\n| Case | Result |\r\n| --- | --- |\r\n| optional arg never set, defaults to `None` | omitted (the fix) |\r\n| optional arg explicitly passed as `None` | kept |\r\n| unset arg with a real schema default (e.g. `limit: int = 10`) | still filled in |\r\n| extra kwargs not in the schema | still stripped |\r\n| missing required arg | still raises `ValueError(\"... validation failed ...\")` |\r\n\r\n`run()` and `arun()` both go through `_validate_kwargs`, so both paths are covered.\r\n\r\n### Why not plain `model_dump(exclude_unset=True)`?\r\n\r\nIt would also drop unset fields that have a real default, so a tool whose `_run` relies on the schema supplying `limit=10` would stop receiving it. Filtering only unset **and** `None` fields fixes the reported bug with the smallest behavior change.\r\n\r\n### Scope\r\n\r\nThis PR does not touch `pydantic_schema_utils._json_schema_to_pydantic_field`, which wraps non-required properties in `Optional[...]`, the second contributing cause noted in the issue. With this change those fields no longer reach the server unless set, which resolves the reported failure. Happy to follow up on the schema generation separately if maintainers want it.\r\n\r\n## Testing\r\n\r\nNew tests in `lib/crewai/tests/tools/test_base_tool.py`:\r\n\r\n- unset optional arg defaulting to `None` is omitted (`run` and `arun`)\r\n- explicit `None` is still sent\r\n- non-`None` schema default is still applied for an unset arg\r\n\r\nResults on my machine:\r\n\r\n- With the fix, the new sync tests pass; with the fix reverted, the \"omitted\" and \"non-`None` default\" tests fail, so they catch the bug.\r\n- `ruff check`, `ruff format --check` and `mypy` are clean on the touched files.\r\n- A static scan of `lib/crewai` and `lib/crewai-tools` found no tool whose `_run` has a required parameter whose schema default is `None` (the one pattern this change could break). The scan only matches schemas defined in the same file as the tool.\r\n- Update: the repo's `--block-network` pytest option stops the asyncio event loop from starting on Windows, so my first run could not execute any `arun` test. Re-running with that option overridden on my command line only (`-o addopts=...`), all 53 tests in `tests/tools/test_base_tool.py` pass, including the new `arun` test.\r\n- I did not run the strict MCP server from the issue end to end.\r\n\r\n## Notes for reviewers\r\n\r\n- The diff is 11 lines of source plus tests. The only behavior change is the one in the table above.\r\n- #8175 (nested input models, #8174) edits the same `model_dump()` line in `_validate_kwargs`. The two changes are compatible; whichever lands second needs a trivial rebase, and I'm happy to do it.\r\n- An earlier PR for this issue (#7900) was closed by its author on Oct 28 and was never reviewed here. This PR takes the same direction (`exclude_unset`-style) with the schema-default behavior preserved.\r\n\r\n## AI disclosure\r\n\r\nThis PR was developed with the assistance of an AI coding agent (Claude Code) under human review, as described in the contributing guide, and should carry the `llm-generated` label. I could not set the label as an external contributor, so please add it.\r\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Medium Risk**\n> Changes validated tool kwargs for every `run`/`arun` call, but the filter is narrow and covered by regression tests; main impact is fixing MCP forwarding without altering explicit-null or default-value semantics.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Fixes **#7891** by changing how `BaseTool._validate_kwargs` builds the kwargs passed to `_run` / `_arun` after Pydantic validation. Instead of a full `model_dump()`, it now **drops** fields that were **not** in `model_fields_set` **and** validate to `None`, so optional parameters the caller never set are no longer forwarded as explicit JSON `null` (a common failure mode for strict MCP tool schemas).\n> \n> **Explicit `None`**, **required fields**, **schema defaults** (e.g. `limit=10`), and **stripping extra LLM kwargs** behave as before. Both **`run()`** and **`arun()`** use this path, including decorator-based `Tool` instances.\n> \n> New tests in `test_base_tool.py` cover omitted unset optional `None` defaults, preserved explicit `None`, and retained non-`None` defaults for sync and async execution.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 79121e78aae4e864f2e40eb77f3bb7809830ae77. Bugbot is set up for automated code reviews on this repo. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->",
